    "title": "<p>Clinical, radiographical, and pathological features of evolving myositis ossificans</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Brittany J. Holmes",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 708.7pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"945\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Feature</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Early</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Intermediate</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Mature</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">Approximate time course</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Initial 3&ndash;6&nbsp;weeks</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">4&ndash;8&nbsp;weeks</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">8&nbsp;weeks &ndash; 6&nbsp;months</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Radiographical findings</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Soft tissue mass without calcification</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Oedema of surrounding tissues</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Zonal pattern: peripheral rim of calcification, initially flocculent then becoming coarse; lucent centre</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Oedema of surrounding tissues</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Periosteal reaction of adjacent bone may be present with retained plane between bone and lesion</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Dense peripheral calcification with lucent or lightly calcified centre</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">Histopathology</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Spindle cell proliferation with granulation tissue and extravasated erythrocytes</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>May be associated with organizing haematoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Zonal pattern: peripheral mature lamellar bone; intermediate osteoblastic proliferation with osteoid mineralizing to woven bone (may have cartilage with enchondral ossification); central non-ossified spindle cell proliferation with prominent vasculature</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Predominantly lamellar bone</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Focal residual woven bone and spindle cell proliferation centrally</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Cytopathology</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Spindle cells with wispy tapered or stellate cytoplasm, ovoid nuclei, smooth nuclear contours, fine chromatin, and increased mitotic activity</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Haemorrhagic or myxoid background with granular debris</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Degenerating or atrophic muscle fibres</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Foamy or haemosiderin-laden histiocytes may be present</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Osteoblasts and multinucleated osteoclast-like giant cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Spindle cells, similar to early phase</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Uninucleated or binucleated chondrocytes may be present</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Amorphous or fibrillary metachromatic stroma consistent with osteoid or chondroid matrix</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Paucicellular sample</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Osteoblasts and osteoclast-like giant cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Fragments of osteoid and mineralized bone</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Adipocytes from marrow fat may be present</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
